{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00086",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 4.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.98,
      "end_seconds": 9.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.74,
      "end_seconds": 28.63,
      "duration_seconds": 17.89,
      "text": "Doctor, it's tightness in my chest when I walk. It's getting on my nerves now. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.44,
      "end_seconds": 32.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "So, do you notice anything setting it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.13,
      "end_seconds": 36.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Yes, walking fast. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.8,
      "end_seconds": 39.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.25,
      "end_seconds": 46.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly. Well, um, and I've been sweating with it as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.83,
      "end_seconds": 49.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Any pain at rest, palpitations or fainting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.24,
      "end_seconds": 52.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "No, um, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.31,
      "end_seconds": 58.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.57,
      "end_seconds": 67.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.02,
      "end_seconds": 74.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.68,
      "end_seconds": 87.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "Uh, uh, not with me. I'll bring it next time. Yeah, I'm on glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.15,
      "end_seconds": 91.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Alright, do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.09,
      "end_seconds": 99.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Oh, um, just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.2,
      "end_seconds": 104.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.49,
      "end_seconds": 112.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.09,
      "end_seconds": 114.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.46,
      "end_seconds": 118.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Uh, I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 130.78,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.27,
      "end_seconds": 145.72,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.05,
      "end_seconds": 148.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.7,
      "end_seconds": 153.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.26,
      "end_seconds": 159.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.92,
      "end_seconds": 162.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.42,
      "end_seconds": 165.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.06,
      "end_seconds": 168.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I mean, my brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.28,
      "end_seconds": 172.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Alright, do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.94,
      "end_seconds": 176.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.95,
      "end_seconds": 180.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.83,
      "end_seconds": 191.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.6,
      "text": "I mean, yes, I had a C-section, about ten years ago. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.77,
      "end_seconds": 199.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.01,
      "end_seconds": 212.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 214.53,
      "end_seconds": 222.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 149 over 89, temperature is 36.7 degrees, pulse 93. SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.12,
      "end_seconds": 224.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.9,
      "end_seconds": 230.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.59,
      "end_seconds": 233.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.51,
      "end_seconds": 248.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.65,
      "end_seconds": 254.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.6,
      "end_seconds": 276.66,
      "duration_seconds": 20.06,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is angina-type chest pain. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.18,
      "end_seconds": 281.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Well, um, should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.69,
      "end_seconds": 297.4,
      "duration_seconds": 14.71,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now angina-type chest pain is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk, moderate, and no palpitations or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.56,
      "end_seconds": 300.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "That's it, uh, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.31,
      "end_seconds": 304.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.2,
      "end_seconds": 312.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, uh, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.82,
      "end_seconds": 333.96,
      "duration_seconds": 21.14,
      "text": "We should do a treadmill test for exertional chest tightness. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's use GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. That's for chest tightness. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.62,
      "end_seconds": 335.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.48,
      "end_seconds": 348.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "I'd like you to take atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for cardiovascular risk. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.51,
      "end_seconds": 350.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.81,
      "end_seconds": 357.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.29,
      "end_seconds": 377.13,
      "duration_seconds": 19.84,
      "text": "Alright. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.44,
      "end_seconds": 379.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.14,
      "end_seconds": 390.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.22,
      "end_seconds": 393.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.77,
      "end_seconds": 401.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Come back after the results are back. Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.92,
      "end_seconds": 414.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "So, I take the GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes and take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.95,
      "end_seconds": 418.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.43,
      "end_seconds": 422.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}